    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d131">

                <pb facs="0219" n="115" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg115"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/3723: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy (Garrett) to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rome</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-01-30T13:00:00+01:00">January 30, 1932—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received January 30—9:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>19. Foreign Office informs me that it is understood that British Government last
                    night made representations in regard to Shanghai <pb facs="0220" n="116"
                        xml:id="pg116"/> through Japanese Ambassador in London and that the Italian
                    Government is disposed to follow the British lead.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Garrett</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
